        "0.5x^2 + 4x - 6",
        "(x^2 + 8x - 12)/2"
      ],
      "display_tex": "y = \\frac{x^2}{2} + 4x - 6",
      "input": "expression"
    },
    "hints": [
      "The variables are already separate: write dy = (x + 4) dx and integrate both sides.",
      "The general solution is y = x²/2 + 4x + c. Substitute x = 2 and y = 4 to find c.",
      "4 = 2 + 8 + c, so c = −6."
    ],
    "solution": [
      {
        "text": "Integrate both sides.",
        "tex": "y = \\int (x + 4)\\,dx = \\frac{x^2}{2} + 4x + c"
