        ]
      },
      "accepted": [
        "y = (1 + x)/(1 - x)",
        "(x + 1)/(1 - x)",
        "-(x + 1)/(x - 1)"
      ],
      "display_tex": "y = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - x}",
      "input": "expression"
    },
    "hints": [
      "Separate the variables: dy/(1 + y²) = dx/(1 + x²).",
      "Both sides integrate to inverse tangents: tan⁻¹ y = tan⁻¹ x + c. Use y(0) = 1 to find c.",
      "c = tan⁻¹ 1 = π/4, so y = tan(tan⁻¹ x + π/4). Expand it with the tangent addition formula."
    ],
    "solution": [
      {
        "text": "Separate the variables and integrate.",
        "tex": "\\int \\frac{dy}{1 + y^2} = \\int \\frac{dx}{1 + x^2} \\implies \\tan^{-1} y = \\tan^{-1} x + c"
      },
      {
        "text": "Use y(0) = 1.",
        "tex": "\\tan^{-1} 1 = 0 + c \\implies c = \\frac{\\pi}{4}"
      },
      {
        "text": "Take the tangent of both sides and use tan(A + B) = (tan A + tan B)/(1 − tan A tan B).",
        "tex": "y = \\tan\\left(\\tan^{-1} x + \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = \\frac{x + 1}{1 - x}"
      }
    ],
    "review": {
      "status": "developer-test",
      "reviewed_by": null,
      "date": null
    }
